X:4
T:Rama's lullaby
T:Maratha lullaby
C:traditional (Maharashtra)
O:India, Maharashtra
R:devotional lullaby
S:Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (1914), Ex. 161, p. 66
N:A Marathi lullaby to the infant Rama as the god Vishnu, sung to Fox Strangways (Adagio, crotchet 80) by a Hindu lady in Calcutta, with his English singing words; each of the four verses ends in the refrain "Little babe, sleep upon my knee". It is a devotional song: schools follow their own guidance on religious songs. Bars 4 and 5 as first read did not add up to two bars of 3/4, so here "born" is shortened to an eighth note and the barline moved, which puts the rest and "Little" at the end of bar 5 as at the end of bar 2; the rest after the last note is dropped. Bars 4 to 6 and the refrain's second bar are still to be checked against the plate.
Q:1/4=80
M:3/4
L:1/16
K:C
