CC | D4 G3 F D3 C | C4 z2 CC D2F2 | G8 z2 FG |
w: In A-yo-dhya, the land of kings, It was Vish-nu's self That was
A2F2 G3 F G3 F | D3 C C4 z2 CC |
w: born on the lap of Kau-shal-ya._ Lit-tle
D4 G3 F D2C2 | D3 C C8 |]
w: babe sleep up-on my knee!__
W:2. For the cradle is wrought of gold, And a Child therein, Of the whole world the Lord and Master, sleeps.
W:   Little babe, sleep upon my knee!
W:3. In the hand-hold of Kaushalya Is the cradle-cord, And the cord is the thread of Bodhana (knowledge).
W:   Little babe, sleep upon my knee!
W:4. And the Devis (goddesses) are strewing flowers From the highest heaven, And with each flower a blessing.
W:   Little babe, sleep upon my knee!

