T:Lalishrita
T:Tamil lullaby, from a phonogram
C:traditional (Tamil Nadu)
O:India, Tamil Nadu (Srirangam)
R:devotional lullaby
S:Fox Strangways, The Music of Hindostan (1914), Ex. 155, p. 64
N:A Tamil lullaby that lays the baby in the care of Sriranga (Vishnu, worshipped at Srirangam), taken down from a phonogram; the words are Fox Strangways's English singing translation, not the Tamil. It is a devotional song: schools follow their own guidance on religious songs. Sing it slowly and freely, holding the fermatas. No tonic is marked; the tune circles G and ends on C, so the drone is on C. Guessed: in bar 3 the two quick notes before "dle" are written as grace notes, and in bar 4 the c on "bright" is a dotted eighth, so that both bars come out whole; the five-note run on "my" (bar 2) and the rhythm of bars 7 and 8 are best readings still to be checked against the plate.
